// Generated from sw5e_source/background.json (structured skills)
const SW5E_BACKGROUNDS = [{"name":"(Un)Retired Adventurer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Insight, Lore, and Survival","skills":["Athletics","Insight","Lore","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of artisan's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Empathic","Loremaster","Survivalist","Crafter","Linguist","Athlete","Observant"],"featureName":"Bridges Not Yet Burned","featureText":"Throughout your adventures you have established a multitude of contacts from all walks of life, but the intervening years have seen those relationships strained. You may use any feature of any other background, but once a particular feature is used, that feature can't be used again until one year has passed.","effects":[{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"rests","title":"Bridges Not Yet Burned","text":"Use any feature of any other background (each individual feature usable 1/year)."}]},{"name":"Addict","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Performance, Persuasion, and Sleight of Hand","skills":["Deception","Performance","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of any gaming set, brewer's kit, or spicer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Performer","Charmer","Quick-Fingered","Competitor","Specialist","Linguist","Durable"],"featureName":"Addicted","featureText":"You've been abusing substances for a long time. You always know who to talk to and where to find substances, and you can often identify them in their raw form.","effects":[]},{"name":"Agent","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Investigation, Lore, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Investigation","Lore","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Investigator","Loremaster","Charmer","Linguist","Alert","Observant","Practiced"],"featureName":"Safe Haven","featureText":"As a faction agent, you have access to a secret network of supporters and operatives who can provide assistance on your adventures. You know a set of secret signs and passwords you can use to identify such operatives, who can provide you with access to a hidden safe house, free room and board, or assistance in finding information. These agents never risk their lives for you or risk revealing their true identities.","effects":[]},{"name":"Amnesiac","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Investigation, and Survival","skills":["Deception","Insight","Investigation","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Choose one from disguise kit, forgery kit, or tinker's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Investigator","Survivalist","Specialist","Crafter","Linguist","Practiced"],"featureName":"A Life Once Lived","featureText":"You once had a home, a family, relationships, possessions, but now you are left with nothing but the ability to start anew. You are unfamiliar with the world around you as well as the people in it. You may often need to ask for clarification on things other adventurers may know intrinsically. Some events, locations, names, phrases, or objects may also trigger you to recall small details which could relate to the life you once had, at the discretion of the GM.","effects":[]},{"name":"Archaeologist","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Investigation, Lore, Perception, or Survival","skills":["Investigation","Lore","Perception","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Surveyor's implements or scavenging kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Investigator","Loremaster","Perceptive","Survivalist","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Dungeon Delver"],"featureName":"Historical Knowledge","featureText":"When you enter a ruin or dungeon, you can correctly ascertain its original purpose and determine its builders, whether those were jedi, sith, hutts, rakata, or some other known species or civilization. Additionally, you can readily determine the value of ancient art.","effects":[]},{"name":"Barbarian","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Athletics, Nature, and Survival","skills":["Animal Handling","Athletics","Nature","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of musical instrument or artisan's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Brawny","Naturalist","Survivalist","Entertainer","Crafter","Athlete","Weapon Expert"],"featureName":"Barbarian Heritage","featureText":"You have an excellent knowledge of not only your tribe's territory, but also the terrain and natural resources of the rest of the worlds. You are familiar enough with any wilderness area that you find twice as much food and water as you normally would when you forage there.\n\nAdditionally, you can call upon the hospitality of other tribes in times of need.","effects":[{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"rests","title":"Barbarian Heritage","text":"Find 2× normal food and water when foraging in any wilderness; call upon other tribes' hospitality."}]},{"name":"Bartender","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Intimidation, Medicine, or Persuasion","skills":["Insight","Intimidation","Medicine","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"Brewer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Threatening","Medic","Charmer","Specialist","Linguist","Observant","Snappy Interjection"],"featureName":"Social Lubricant","featureText":"You have no trouble finding and getting into places that serve drinks. While drinking in a social establishment, strangers take a liking to you and feel comfortable enough to share gossip.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Brewer's kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Blackguard","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Lore, and Survival","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Lore","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Artificer's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Loremaster","Survivalist","Crafter","Linguist","Formfighting Dabbler","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"Student of the Force","featureText":"You often know where to find information on Force-sensitive organizations, or where to find someone who would know, and can readily decipher more common lore about them. Your GM might rule that the knowledge you seek is secreted away in an almost inaccessible place, that it simply cannot be found, or is too difficult to decipher.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Artificer's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Bodyguard","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Insight, Investigation, and Perception","skills":["Athletics","Insight","Investigation","Perception"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of demolitions kit, disguise kit, or security kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Empathic","Investigator","Perceptive","Specialist","Linguist","Athlete","Durable"],"featureName":"Authorized Violence","featureText":"As a licensed professional, most law enforcement tend to turn a blind eye when you are involved in altercations. You are rarely detained due to wearing armor and wielding weaponry; in fact, while accompanying your client, it is typically socially acceptable for you to go both armed and armored.","effects":[]},{"name":"Bounty Hunter","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Persuasion, and Stealth","skills":["Deception","Insight","Persuasion","Stealth"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Charmer","Stealthy","Specialist","Linguist","Alert","Athlete"],"featureName":"Ear to the Ground","featureText":"You are in frequent contact with people in the segment of society that your chosen quarries move through. These people might be associated with the criminal underworld, the rough-and-tumble folk of the streets, or members of high society. This connection comes in the form of a contact in any city you visit, a person who provides information about the people and places of the local area.","effects":[]},{"name":"City Watch","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Insight, Investigation, and Perception","skills":["Athletics","Insight","Investigation","Perception"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Empathic","Investigator","Perceptive","Linguist","Alert","Athlete","Durable"],"featureName":"Watcher's Eye","featureText":"Your experience in enforcing the law, and dealing with lawbreakers, gives you a feel for local laws and criminals. You can easily find the local outpost of the watch or a similar organization, and just as easily pick out the dens of criminal activity in a community, although you're more likely to be welcome in the former locations rather than the latter.","effects":[]},{"name":"Clone","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Lore, Sleight of Hand and Survival","skills":["Athletics","Lore","Sleight of Hand","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of geneticist's implements, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Athlete","Loremaster","Quick-Fingered","Survivalist","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"A Life Not Lived","featureText":"Being a clone, you were born from the existence of another. Flashes of deeds you never did, of people you have never met and of information you have never learned sporadically appear. You may be confused with your DNA-Donor by others, being befriended by, or made enemies of, people you have never before met. The exact nature of these revelations depends on the nature of your DNA-Donor; they might lead to a site that only one other has ever seen, some long-forgotten fact, relic or weapon from the past that could reshape the present, or even information that would be damaging to the people who created you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Clone Trooper","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Medicine, Perception, and Piloting","skills":["Athletics","Medicine","Perception","Piloting"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Medic","Perceptive","Ace Pilot","Specialist","Alert","Athlete","Forceful Vigor"],"featureName":"Republic Rank","featureText":"You are a soldier of the Republic. Those loyal to the Republic will respect your status and defer to you if they don't outrank you. You can invoke your position to exert influence over other soldiers, requisition simple equipment, and gain access to military compounds affiliated with the Republic.","effects":[]},{"name":"Companion","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Acrobatics, Deception, Insight, and Performance","skills":["Acrobatics","Deception","Insight","Performance"],"toolProficiencies":"One instrument of your choice or a disguise kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Acrobat","Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Performer","Entertainer","Specialist","Linguist","Force of Personality"],"featureName":"Sordid Knowledge","featureText":"You have or can gain compromising information about people of importance. You may be able to leverage this information in order to acquire lodging, information, or even money.  You may also become a target for having this information. Your GM may rule that any particular individual is either above reproach or is too careful in covering their tracks to provide such leverage.","effects":[]},{"name":"Courtier","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Performance, and Survival","skills":["Deception","Insight","Performance","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Performer","Survivalist","Linguist","Actor","Practiced","Force of Personality"],"featureName":"Court Functionality","featureText":"Your knowledge of how bureaucracies function lets you gain access to the records and inner workings of any noble court or government you encounter. You know who the movers and shakers are, whom to go to for the favors you seek, and what the current intrigues of interest in the group are.","effects":[]},{"name":"Crime Lord","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Insight","Intimidation","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Threatening","Charmer","Competitor","Linguist","Inspiring Leader","Observant"],"featureName":"Criminal Network","featureText":"You have access to an extensive network of organised crime. You know how to get messages to and from local contacts, even over great distances; you know the local messengers, corrupt caravan masters, and seedy sailors who can deliver messages for you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Criminal","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Intimidation, Sleight of Hand, and Stealth","skills":["Deception","Intimidation","Sleight of Hand","Stealth"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set, your choice of demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Threatening","Quick-Fingered","Stealthy","Competitor","Specialist","Feigned Confidence","Observant"],"featureName":"Criminal Contact","featureText":"You have a reliable and trustworthy contact who acts as your liaison to a network of other criminals. You know how to get messages to and from your contact, even over great distances; specifically, you know the local messengers, corrupt caravan masters, and seedy sailors who can deliver messages for you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Dathomir Witch","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Acrobatics, Animal Handling, Lore, and Nature","skills":["Acrobatics","Animal Handling","Lore","Nature"],"toolProficiencies":"Bioanalysis kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Acrobat","Animal Handler","Loremaster","Naturalist","Specialist","Linguist","Force-Sensitive","Force of Personality"],"featureName":"Matriarchal Society","featureText":"Other Dathomir Witches know, and will look out for you. If you're ever in need of a place to stay, or a meal to eat, other Dathomir Witches will help you as long as your clans aren't feuding. This could be in the form of shelters, meals, even healing. If the Dathomir Witches are of your clan or a clan friendly to you, they may be willing to help you even at cost to themselves.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Bioanalysis kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Entertainer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Acrobatics, Insight, Performance, and Sleight of Hand","skills":["Acrobatics","Insight","Performance","Sleight of Hand"],"toolProficiencies":"Disguise kit, one type of musical instrument","languages":"","featOptions":["Acrobat","Empathic","Performer","Quick-Fingered","Specialist","Entertainer","Practiced","Actor"],"featureName":"By Popular Demand","featureText":"You can always find a place to perform, usually in an inn or cantina but possibly with a circus, at a theater, or even in a noble's court. At such a place, you receive free lodging and food of a modest or comfortable standard (depending on the quality of the establishment), as long as you perform each night. In addition, your performance makes you something of a local figure. When strangers recognize you in a town where you have performed, they typically take a liking to you.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Disguise kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Ex-Cultist","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Intimidation, Investigation, or Lore","skills":["Deception","Intimidation","Investigation","Lore"],"toolProficiencies":"Poisoner's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Threatening","Investigator","Loremaster","Specialist","Linguist","Galvanizing Presence","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"Secret Signs","featureText":"You know the secret symbology of your cult, which can pop up in some surprising places. With a subtle gesture or knowing handshake you can discern who follows the ways of your dark lord. Cloisters of your cult may be hidden across the galaxy, identified by the secret signs and symbols designed to lead the faithful to places of dark worship. Such cloistered often contain enough lodging and food for at least ten people, for a week, and sometimes harbor eldritch treasures belonging to the cult.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Poisoner's kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Faction Adventurer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Investigation, Nature, and Survival","skills":["Athletics","Investigation","Nature","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Investigator","Naturalist","Survivalist","Specialist","Linguist","Alert","Athlete"],"featureName":"Faction Membership","featureText":"You are an established and respected member of an adventurer's faction, allowing you to rely on certain benefits that membership provides. If you are in a town with a headquarters for your adventurer's faction and you are in good standing with the faction, you will be allowed to look at the job postings and find adventuring work to earn money. \n\nfactions often wield tremendous political power. If you are accused of a crime, your faction will support you if a good case can be made for your innocence or the crime is justifiable. You can also gain access to powerful political figures through the faction, if you are a member in good standing. You must pay dues of 50 cr per month to the faction. Your dues must be current to remain in the faction's good graces.","effects":[]},{"name":"Faction Artisan","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Insight, Persuasion, and Technology","skills":["Athletics","Insight","Persuasion","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of artisan's implements, biochemist's kit, or chef's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Empathic","Charmer","Techie","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Haggler"],"featureName":"Faction Membership","featureText":"As an established and respected member of a faction, you can rely on certain benefits that membership provides. Your fellow faction members will provide you with lodging and food if necessary, and pay for your funeral if needed. In some cities and towns, a factionhall offers a central place to meet other members of your profession, which can be a good place to meet potential patrons, allies, or hirelings.\n\nfactions often wield tremendous political power. If you are accused of a crime, your faction will support you if a good case can be made for your innocence or the crime is justifiable. You can also gain access to powerful political figures through the faction, if you are a member in good standing. You must pay dues of 50 cr per month to the faction. Your dues must be current to remain in the faction's good graces.","effects":[]},{"name":"Faction Merchant","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Performance, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Insight","Performance","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Performer","Charmer","Linguist","Haggler","Inspiring Leader","Practiced"],"featureName":"Faction Membership","featureText":"As an established and respected member of a faction, you can rely on certain benefits that membership provides. Your fellow faction members will provide you with lodging and food if necessary, and pay for your funeral if needed. In some cities and towns, a factionhall offers a central place to meet other members of your profession, which can be a good place to meet potential patrons, allies, or hirelings.\n\nfactions often wield tremendous political power. If you are accused of a crime, your faction will support you if a good case can be made for your innocence or the crime is justifiable. You can also gain access to powerful political figures through the faction, if you are a member in good standing. You must pay dues of 50 cr per month to the faction. Your dues must be current to remain in the faction's good graces.","effects":[]},{"name":"Far Traveler","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Perception, and Persuasion","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Perception","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"One musical instrument or gaming set of your choice","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Perceptive","Charmer","Entertainer","Competitor","Linguist","Practiced"],"featureName":"All Eyes On You","featureText":"Your foreign nature attracts attention, yielding access to people and places you might not otherwise have, for you and your traveling companions. Noble lords, scholars, and merchant princes, to name a few, might be interested in hearing about your distant homeland and people.","effects":[]},{"name":"Farmer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Nature, Persuasion, and Technology","skills":["Animal Handling","Nature","Persuasion","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One instrument and one type of artisan's implements or bioanalysis kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Naturalist","Charmer","Techie","Entertainer","Crafter","Specialist","Haggler"],"featureName":"Rustic Hospitality","featureText":"Since you are of the common folk, you fit in among them with ease. You can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate among other commoners, unless you have shown yourself to be a danger to them. They will shield you from the law or anyone else searching for you, though they will not risk their lives for you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Folk Hero","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Athletics, Nature, and Performance","skills":["Animal Handling","Athletics","Nature","Performance"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of artisan's implements, biochemist's kit, or chef's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Brawny","Naturalist","Performer","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Healer"],"featureName":"Rustic Hospitality","featureText":"Since you are of the common folk, you fit in among them with ease. You can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate among other commoners, unless you have shown yourself to be a danger to them. They will shield you from the law or anyone else searching for you, though they will not risk their lives for you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Force Adept","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Perception, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Insight","Perception","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"Two of your choice of artisan's implements, gaming sets, or musical instruments","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Perceptive","Charmer","Crafter","Competitor","Entertainer","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"Guided by the Force","featureText":"When you attempt to learn a piece of knowledge, you often instinctively know where or from whom you can obtain it. Usually, this information comes from a seemingly random person, book, or data file. Your GM might rule that the knowledge you seek is secreted away in an almost inaccessible place, or that it simply cannot be found.","effects":[]},{"name":"Gambler","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Sleight of Hand","skills":["Deception","Insight","Intimidation","Sleight of Hand"],"toolProficiencies":"Two types of gaming sets","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Threatening","Quick-Fingered","Competitor","Keen Mind","Observant","Practiced"],"featureName":"Let's Make It Interesting","featureText":"You can convince nearly anyone to put up something they aren't normally willing to part with (property or information) in a game of chance. Your GM might rule that they will only agree to a game of their choosing, and they may only agree if they feel the odds are in their favor.","effects":[]},{"name":"Gladiator","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Acrobatics, Athletics, Intimidation, and Performance","skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Intimidation","Performance"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of musical instrument","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Acrobat","Brawny","Threatening","Performer","Entertainer","Linguist","Athlete","Durable"],"featureName":"A Champion Well Known","featureText":"You can always find a place to perform, usually in an inn or tavern but possibly with a circus, at a theater, or even in a noble's court. At such a place, you receive free lodging and food of a modest or comfortable standard (depending on the quality of the establishment), as long as you perform each night. In addition, your performance makes you something of a local figure. When strangers recognize you in a town where you have performed, they typically take a liking to you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Hermit","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Lore, Medicine, and Nature","skills":["Animal Handling","Lore","Medicine","Nature"],"toolProficiencies":"Bioanalysis kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Loremaster","Medic","Naturalist","Specialist","Alert","Dungeon Delver","Healer"],"featureName":"Discovery","featureText":"The seclusion of your hermitage gave you access to a unique and powerful discovery. The nature of this revelation depends on the nature of your seclusion. You might have discovered a great truth about the cosmos or the Force, a fact that has long been forgotten, a relic of the past that could rewrite history, or a place unseen for ages. It might be information that would be damaging to the people who consigned you to exile, and hence the reason for your return to society. Work with your GM to determine the details of your discovery and its impact on the campaign.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Bioanalysis kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Holonet Technician","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Stealth, and Technology","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Stealth","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"Choose two from mechanic's kit, security kit, and slicer's kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Stealthy","Techie","Specialist","Keen Mind","Practiced","Tech Dabbler"],"featureName":"Holonet Access","featureText":"You have the codes to a distributor station which gives you access to all information sent through it. This information comes in the form of useful (and sometimes sensitive) information on a topic you choose each day to tune into; this information isn't always reliable or interesting. Regardless of the quality of the information, it's relevance most likely pertains to your locale.","effects":[]},{"name":"Imperial Knight","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Intimidation, Perception, or Piloting","skills":["Athletics","Intimidation","Perception","Piloting"],"toolProficiencies":"Armormech's implements and artificer's implements","languages":"","featOptions":["Brawny","Threatening","Perceptive","Ace Pilot","Crafter","Force-Sensitive","Armor Expert","Weapon Expert"],"featureName":"Will of the Emperor","featureText":"The authority granted by your position is easily acknowledged even by those who don't recognize the Imperial Knights. Though they might not know you, common citizens will extend you every courtesy and do their utmost to help you. Unless you have shown yourself to be a danger to them, they will even take up arms to fight alongside you, should you find yourself facing an enemy alone.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Armormech's implements","rank":1},{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Artificer's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Independent Droid","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Medicine, Persuasion, or Technology","skills":["Athletics","Medicine","Persuasion","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"Astrotech's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Medic","Charmer","Techie","Crafter","Linguist","Shard Modification","Customized Droid"],"featureName":"Deviant Knowledge","featureText":"When you served under a master, you would often hear secrets that weren't meant for your ears. Back then, however, you weren't alive. You have insider knowledge on your previous owner or perhaps others who passed through your area. This knowledge may be used for leverage, revenge, or other means, at the discretion of your GM. This knowledge, while it may prove useful in your adventure, may also make you a target for those whose secrets you possess.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Astrotech's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Insurgent","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Persuasion, Stealth, or Technology","skills":["Insight","Persuasion","Stealth","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of artisan's implements, disguise kit, or forgery kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Charmer","Stealthy","Techie","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Alert"],"featureName":"Rebel Kinship","featureText":"You are part of a network of fellow insurgents. Although you may not always agree on the methods of dissent with your fellow members, they are willing to create distractions in public, provide safe passage, and inform you of the patrol routes of guards, the military and other law enforcement in the cities and territories in which they are active.","effects":[]},{"name":"Investigator","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Perception, and Survival","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Perception","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Perceptive","Survivalist","Linguist","Alert","Observant","Keen Mind"],"featureName":"Watcher's Eye","featureText":"Your experience in enforcing the law, and dealing with lawbreakers, gives you a feel for local laws and criminals. You can easily find the local outpost of the watch or a similar organization, and just as easily pick out the dens of criminal activity in a community, although you're more likely to be welcome in the former locations rather than the latter.","effects":[]},{"name":"Jedi","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Lore, and Persuasion","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Lore","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"Artificer's tools","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Loremaster","Charmer","Linguist","Crafter","Formfighting Dabbler","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"Shelter of the Faithful","featureText":"As a Jedi, you command the respect of those who are loyal to the Jedi Order. You and your adventuring companions can expect to receive free healing and care at any Jedi temple, and those who support your religion will support you (but only you) at a modest lifestyle.\n\nYou might also have ties to a specific Jedi temple and have a residence there. This could be the temple where you trained, or a temple where you have found a new home. While near your temple, you can call upon the Jedi for assistance, provided the assistance you ask for is not hazardous and you remain in good standing with your temple.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Artificer's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Jensaarai","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Intimidation, Lore, and Perception","skills":["Insight","Intimidation","Lore","Perception"],"toolProficiencies":"Armormech's implements","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Threatening","Loremaster","Perceptive","Crafter","Linguist","Alert","Observant"],"featureName":"Depths of Duality","featureText":"Due to the corruption of the Jedi training done to the pre-Jensaarai, you have a unique insight into both the Light and Dark side of the Force, as well as its history, applications, and techniques in a scholarly manner.\n\nYou are well versed in the above concepts, and can recall key information related to them. However, if the research was hidden from the public and you have not had experience working with it, you can only partially understand it. You also recognize well-known Jedi Masters and Sith Lords by their works and marks.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Armormech's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Jizz Wailer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Performance, Persuasion, and Sleight of Hand","skills":["Insight","Performance","Persuasion","Sleight of Hand"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of musical instrument","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Performer","Charmer","Quick-Fingered","Entertainer","Linguist","Feigned Confidence","Snappy Interjection"],"featureName":"Steady Gig","featureText":"You can always find a place to perform, usually in an cantina or spice den but possibly in a fine dining establishment, culture center or even a noble's court. At such a place, you receive free lodging and food of a modest or comfortable standard (depending on the quality of the establishment), as long as you perform each night. In addition, your performance makes you something of a local figure. When strangers recognize you in a town where you have performed, they typically take a liking to you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Laborer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Athletics, Survival, and Technology","skills":["Animal Handling","Athletics","Survival","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set and one set of artisan's implements","languages":"","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Brawny","Survivalist","Techie","Competitor","Crafter","Athlete","Durable"],"featureName":"Working Class","featureText":"You have a contact that acts as your liaison to a union or faction. You know how to reach your contact at all times. Your contact can provide you with the means to requisition equipment used in manufacturing or shipping.","effects":[]},{"name":"Lawyer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Performance, and Persuasion","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Performance","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Performer","Charmer","Linguist","Actor","Observant","Keen Mind"],"featureName":"Legal Authority","featureText":"You are familiar with the letter of the law and workings of courts, at least on the planet that you were a judge in. If you are in a foreign place where you are not familiar with their exact laws, you often will be able to track down the resources you need to learn them. \n\nIf you or your party gets into legal trouble, your experience may help you get out of it. If you can prove your credentials, you might be able to represent your party in a court of law without admonishment. You may know of legal loopholes that will help your case. If you are in the region where you originally worked, you might have past connections with many legal professionals there.","effects":[]},{"name":"Mandalorian","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Intimidation, Piloting, and Survival","skills":["Athletics","Intimidation","Piloting","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"One set of artisan's implements","languages":"Mando'a","featOptions":["Brawny","Threatening","Ace Pilot","Survivalist","Crafter","Durable","Weapon Expert","Athlete"],"featureName":"Child of Mandalore","featureText":"Other Mandalorians know, and will look out for you. If you're ever in need of a place to stay, or a meal to eat, other Mandalorians  will help you as long as your clans aren't feuding. This could be in the form of shelters, meals, even healing. If the Mandalorians are of your clan or a clan friendly to you, they may be willing to help you even at cost to themselves.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"language","target":"Mando'a","rank":1}]},{"name":"Mercenary","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Investigation, Persuasion, and Piloting","skills":["Athletics","Investigation","Persuasion","Piloting"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Investigator","Charmer","Ace Pilot","Competitor","Linguist","Weapon Expert","Durable"],"featureName":"Mercenary Life","featureText":"You know the mercenary life as only someone who has experienced it can. You are able to identify mercenary companies by their emblems, and you know a little about any such company, including the names and reputations of its commanders and leaders, and who has hired them recently. You can find the cantinas and feasthalls where mercenaries abide in any area, as long as you speak the language, and if you spend at least an hour in such a location you can come across one of the following bits of information: a job offer, significant rumor, referral to a skilled merchant, blacksmith, etc., or a hint towards the pursuit of your current quest. Additionally, you can find mercenary work between adventures sufficient to maintain a comfortable lifestyle (see \"Practicing a Profession\" under \"Downtime Activities\" in chapter 8 of the Player's Handbook).","effects":[]},{"name":"Noble","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Lore, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Insight","Lore","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Loremaster","Charmer","Competitor","Linguist","Inspiring Leader","Observant"],"featureName":"Position of Privilege","featureText":"Thanks to your noble birth, people are inclined to think the best of you. You are welcome in high society, and people assume you have the right to be wherever you are. The common folk make every effort to accommodate you and avoid your displeasure, and other people of high birth treat you as a member of the same social sphere. You can secure an audience with a local noble if you need to.","effects":[]},{"name":"Nomad","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Athletics, Medicine, and Survival","skills":["Animal Handling","Athletics","Medicine","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of musical instrument","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Brawny","Medic","Survivalist","Entertainer","Linguist","Dungeon Delver","Observant"],"featureName":"Wanderer","featureText":"You have an excellent memory for maps and geography, and you can always recall the general layout of terrain, settlements, and other features around you. In addition, you can find food and fresh water for yourself and up to five other people each day, provided that the land offers berries, small game, water, and so forth.","effects":[{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"rests","title":"Wanderer","text":"Always recall general map/terrain layout; forage food and fresh water for yourself and up to 5 others daily."}]},{"name":"Office Worker","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Lore, and Perception","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Lore","Perception"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Loremaster","Perceptive","Competitor","Linguist","Feigned Confidence","Snappy Interjection"],"featureName":"Clerical Augur","featureText":"You have an intuitive understanding of how offices work and can readily fit in to an office environment as if you were meant to be there, as long as no one looks too carefully. Additionally, you know where the true power lies in the office: you know who is likely to know the local gossip and you know who to sweet talk into getting things done for you.","effects":[]},{"name":"Outlaw","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Acrobatics, Athletics, Insight, and Survival","skills":["Acrobatics","Athletics","Insight","Survival"],"toolProficiencies":"Disguise kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Acrobat","Brawny","Empathic","Survivalist","Specialist","Linguist","Alert","Observant"],"featureName":"Notorious","featureText":"Since you come from the ranks of the common folk, you fit among them with ease. You can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate among other commoners, unless you've shown yourself to be a danger to them. They will shield you from the law or anyone else searching for you, though they will not risk their lives for you.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Disguise kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Pirate","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Deception, Intimidation, and Piloting","skills":["Athletics","Deception","Intimidation","Piloting"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set, your choice of demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Brawny","Silver-Tongued","Threatening","Ace Pilot","Competitor","Specialist","Feigned Confidence","Force of Personality"],"featureName":"Galactic Scourge","featureText":"You've been from one end of the galaxy to the other. You know the most lucrative trade routes. You have expert knowledge of the various hyperlanes. In addition to this, you know a large number of the models and designs of common space ships that are found in the galaxy. Further, the bonds you formed with your crew are strong, and you can call on their aid even if you've been away from their side for some time. You can expect your former comrades to offer you passage aboard ship, reasonable aid, or shelter when you are in need. Keep in mind that this bond goes both ways, and they may come to you expecting the same.","effects":[]},{"name":"Politician","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Intimidation, Performance, and Persuasion","skills":["Deception","Intimidation","Performance","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice.","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Threatening","Performer","Charmer","Linguist","Actor","Observant","Inspiring Leader"],"featureName":"Political Presence","featureText":"When you walk into a room, people immediately respect your opinion and listen to what you have to say. You are commonly taken for face value as a person of great standing. People will likely treat you like a noble or assume you of that lineage. You can attain audiences with nobles or officials easily, as they may often see you as one of their circle. Bureaucratic red tape holds little challenge to you because you always seem to know the right person to talk to.","effects":[]},{"name":"Racer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Animal Handling, Nature, Piloting, and Technology","skills":["Animal Handling","Nature","Piloting","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set or mechanic's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Animal Handler","Naturalist","Ace Pilot","Techie","Competitor","Specialist","Linguist","Observant"],"featureName":"Terrain Mastery","featureText":"You have a preternatural instinct for understanding the terrain, interpreting maps, and planning routes.  You and your party can move at three-fourths your speed over difficult terrain during long-distance travel.  Because of these skills, if you know your destination and the intervening terrain--either by reputation, by sight, or by maps you have seen--you are able to identify an effective short-cut, trimming your travel time by up to half.  Your GM may rule that your short-cut entails significant danger or may be temporarily impassable.","effects":[{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"defenses","title":"Terrain Mastery","text":"Party moves at 3/4 speed over difficult terrain during long-distance travel; identify shortcuts trimming travel time by up to half."}]},{"name":"Scavenger","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Persuasion, Sleight of Hand, Survival, and Technology","skills":["Persuasion","Sleight of Hand","Survival","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of archaeologist kit, jeweler's implements, mechanic's kit, or scavenging kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Loremaster","Quick-Fingered","Techie","Specialist","Crafter","Linguist","Tech Dabbler"],"featureName":"Rugged Survivalist","featureText":"Scavengers due to their line of work have an eye for spotting useful or even valuable parts of technology or artifacts. You can easily spot the best place to scavenge the most valuable parts.","effects":[]},{"name":"Scientist","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Lore, Medicine, Nature, and Technology","skills":["Lore","Medicine","Nature","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One of your choice","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Loremaster","Medic","Naturalist","Techie","Crafter","Linguist","Tech Dabbler","Keen Mind"],"featureName":"Scientific Method","featureText":"You are well acquainted with your field of research from having read numerous journals or having attended scientific conferences. Concepts that are complicated, involving technical jargon that usually goes over most people's heads, are simple to you. You fully understand concepts, can recall key information, and know how to use equipment related to your field, unless the research was hidden from the public, in which case you may only partially understand it. You also recognize well-known figures in your field.","effects":[]},{"name":"Scoundrel","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Performance, and Sleight of Hand","skills":["Deception","Insight","Performance","Sleight of Hand"],"toolProficiencies":"Disguise Kit, Forgery Kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Performer","Quick-Fingered","Specialist","Force of Personality","Snappy Interjection","Actor"],"featureName":"False Identity","featureText":"You have created a second identity that includes documentation, established acquaintances, and disguises that allow you to assume that persona.\n\nAdditionally, you can forge documents including official papers and personal letters, as long as you have seen an example of the kind of document or the handwriting you are trying to copy.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Disguise kit","rank":1},{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Forgery kit","rank":1}]},{"name":"Servant","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Lore, Performance, and Persuasion","skills":["Insight","Lore","Performance","Persuasion"],"toolProficiencies":"One of your choice","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Loremaster","Performer","Charmer","Crafter","Entertainer","Specialist","Linguist"],"featureName":"Decorum","featureText":"You know how to carry yourself around the elite and their servants. When in the presence of someone of power, or the servants of such a person, you can easily act as if you belong and, barring any extremely outlandish behavior, you can pass off your companions as belonging, too.","effects":[]},{"name":"Sith","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Lore","skills":["Deception","Insight","Intimidation","Lore"],"toolProficiencies":"Artificer's tools","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Threatening","Loremaster","Linguist","Crafter","Formfighting Dabbler","Force-Sensitive"],"featureName":"Feared","featureText":"As a Sith, you instill fear in those who are aware of your standing. When you are in a civilized environment, you can get away with minor criminal offenses, such as refusing to pay for food at a cantina or cutting through doors at a local shop, since most people will not report your activity to the authorities.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Artificer's implements","rank":1}]},{"name":"Smuggler","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Piloting, Sleight of Hand, and Stealth","skills":["Deception","Piloting","Sleight of Hand","Stealth"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set and your choice of demolitions kit, security kit, or slicer's kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Ace Pilot","Quick-Fingered","Stealthy","Competitor","Specialist","Feigned Confidence","Force of Personality"],"featureName":"Careful Selection","featureText":"Some close brushes with the law have taught you that not every city guard can be bribed, and some people are simply too keen to miss minute discrepancies. This feature allows you to study a person and gain insight into whether or not they would accept a bribe, or to pick up on whether they are exceptionally more perceptive than you. It does not reveal how expensive a bribe may be for a given situation, however.","effects":[]},{"name":"Soldier","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Athletics, Intimidation, Persuasion, and Piloting","skills":["Athletics","Intimidation","Persuasion","Piloting"],"toolProficiencies":"One type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Brawny","Threatening","Charmer","Ace Pilot","Competitor","Linguist","Weapon Expert","Healer"],"featureName":"Military Rank","featureText":"You have a military rank from your career as a soldier. Soldiers loyal to your former military organization still recognize your authority and influence, and they defer to you if they are of a lower rank. You can invoke your rank to exert influence over other soldiers and requisition simple equipment for temporary use. You can also usually gain access to friendly military encampments where your rank is recognized.","effects":[]},{"name":"Spacer","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Investigation, Piloting, and Technology","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Piloting","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of chef's kit, mechanic's kit, or one type of gaming set","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Investigator","Ace Pilot","Techie","Specialist","Competitor","Galvanizing Presence","Inspiring Leader"],"featureName":"Well-Traveled","featureText":"As a spacer, you've been from one end of the galaxy to the other. You've traveled along many of the trade routes, and know the safest routes. You have expert knowledge of the various hyperlanes. In addition to this, you know a large number of the models and designs of common space ships that are found in the galaxy.","effects":[]},{"name":"Student","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Insight, Lore, Investigation, and Nature","skills":["Insight","Investigation","Lore","Nature"],"toolProficiencies":"","languages":"Two of your choice","featOptions":["Empathic","Loremaster","Investigator","Naturalist","Linguist","Keen Mind","Observant","Healer"],"featureName":"Library Access","featureText":"Though others must often endure extensive interviews and significant fees to gain access to even the most common archives in your library, you have free and easy access to the majority of the library, though it might also have repositories of lore that are too valuable, powerful, or secret to permit anyone immediate access.\n\nYou have a working knowledge of your cloister's personnel and bureaucracy, and you know how to navigate those connections with some ease.\n\nAdditionally, you are likely to gain preferential treatment at other libraries across the galaxy, as professional courtesy shown to a fellow scholar.","effects":[]},{"name":"Survivor","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Investigation, Lore, Survival, and Technology","skills":["Investigation","Lore","Survival","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"Your choice of artist's implements, biotech's implements, or brewer's kit","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Investigator","Loremaster","Survivalist","Techie","Crafter","Specialist","Linguist","Total Reconstruction"],"featureName":"Heart of Darkness","featureText":"Those who look into your eyes can see that you have faced unimaginable horror and that you are no stranger to darkness. Though they might fear you, commoners will extend you every courtesy and do their utmost to help you. Unless you have shown yourself to be a danger to them, they may even take up arms to fight alongside you, should you find yourself facing an enemy alone.","effects":[]},{"name":"Teacher","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Lore, Nature, Performance, and Technology","skills":["Lore","Nature","Performance","Technology"],"toolProficiencies":"One instrument or set of artisan's implements of your choice","languages":"One of your choice","featOptions":["Loremaster","Naturalist","Performer","Techie","Entertainer","Crafter","Linguist","Feigned Confidence"],"featureName":"Knowledge","featureText":"If you need information on something, you know if there is a book containing that information and where to find it. Further, when you hear a creature speaking or when you see language written down, you can identify exactly what language is being used even if you are not proficient in the language.  Finally, when you hear music, you know which instruments are being used in the performance, even if you are not proficient in their use.","effects":[{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"skills","title":"Knowledge","text":"Know if a book holds needed info and where to find it; identify any spoken/written language and musical instrument without proficiency."}]},{"name":"Urchin","skillProficiencies":"Choose two from Deception, Insight, Sleight of Hand, and Stealth","skills":["Deception","Insight","Sleight of Hand","Stealth"],"toolProficiencies":"Disguise kit, security kit","languages":"","featOptions":["Silver-Tongued","Empathic","Quick-Fingered","Stealthy","Specialist","Alert","Athlete","Observant"],"featureName":"City of Secrets","featureText":"You know the secret patterns and flows to cities and can find passages through the urban sprawl that others would miss. When you are not in combat, you (and companions you lead) can travel between any two locations in the city twice as fast as your speed would normally allow.","effects":[{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Disguise kit","rank":1},{"type":"proficiency","kind":"tool","target":"Security kit","rank":1},{"type":"contextualNote","surface":"defenses","title":"City of Secrets","text":"Out of combat, you and companions you lead travel between any two locations in a city at 2× normal speed."}]}];
